From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: software_isp: debayer shaders: skip the contrast curve when neutral

The GPU debayer applies the contrast S-curve with one pow() per colour
channel on every pixel, even at the default neutral contrast where the curve
is the identity (contrastExp = tan(pi/4) = 1). On the Adreno 306 (SM-T550)
the debayer is the most expensive GPU job per camera frame. Branch on the
uniform and skip the curve when it cannot change anything.

---
--- a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
+++ b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
@@ -288,9 +288,16 @@
 	 * contrastExp 0..2 contrast to 0..infinity; avoid actual infinity at tan(pi/2)
 	 */
 	rgb = clamp(rgb, 0.0, 1.0);
-	rgb.r = apply_contrast(rgb.r);
-	rgb.g = apply_contrast(rgb.g);
-	rgb.b = apply_contrast(rgb.b);
+	/*
+	 * Neutral contrast (the default, contrastExp = tan(pi/4)) is the
+	 * identity: skip three pow() per pixel, which are expensive on small
+	 * GPUs. The branch is uniform, so it costs nothing per fragment.
+	 */
+	if (abs(contrastExp - 1.0) > 0.001) {
+		rgb.r = apply_contrast(rgb.r);
+		rgb.g = apply_contrast(rgb.g);
+		rgb.b = apply_contrast(rgb.b);
+	}
 
 	/* Apply gamma after colour correction */
 	rgb = pow(rgb, vec3(gamma));
--- a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag
+++ b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_unpacked.frag
@@ -145,9 +145,16 @@
      * Contrast
      */
     rgb = clamp(rgb, 0.0, 1.0);
-    rgb.r = apply_contrast(rgb.r);
-    rgb.g = apply_contrast(rgb.g);
-    rgb.b = apply_contrast(rgb.b);
+    /*
+     * Neutral contrast (the default, contrastExp = tan(pi/4)) is the
+     * identity: skip three pow() per pixel, which are expensive on small
+     * GPUs. The branch is uniform, so it costs nothing per fragment.
+     */
+    if (abs(contrastExp - 1.0) > 0.001) {
+        rgb.r = apply_contrast(rgb.r);
+        rgb.g = apply_contrast(rgb.g);
+        rgb.b = apply_contrast(rgb.b);
+    }
 
     /* Apply gamma after colour correction */
     rgb = pow(rgb, vec3(gamma));
